{
    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "PACE_OCI_MI_CLOSE_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The Closed-Loop Ocean Simulation for Evaluation of ocean color retrieval algorithms (CLOSE) Model Input collection provides modeled remote sensing reflectance, inherent optical properties, phytoplankton community composition, and associated environmental variables derived from the NASA Ocean Biogeochemical Model coupled to the Ocean-Atmosphere Spectral Irradiance Model. These data serve as inputs to PyTOAST for simulating PACE OCI Level-1B observations and support end-to-end algorithm development, evaluation, and uncertainty analysis.\n\n Geophysical variables in this suite include:\n - Rrs \u2014 Remote sensing reflectance (sr\u207b\u00b9)\n - a \u2014 Total absorption at selected wavelengths (m\u207b\u00b9)\n - adg \u2014 Absorption due to colored dissolved and detrital material (m\u207b\u00b9)\n - aph \u2014 Absorption due to phytoplankton (m\u207b\u00b9)\n - bb \u2014 Total backscattering (m\u207b\u00b9)\n - bbp \u2014 Particulate backscattering (m\u207b\u00b9)\n - chlor_a \u2014 Total chlorophyll concentration (mg m\u207b\u00b3)\n - chlorophytes, coccolithophores, cyanobacteria, diatoms, dinoflagellates, and phaeocystis \u2014 Phytoplankton community components (mg m\u207b\u00b3)\n - cdom \u2014 Colored dissolved carbon (\u00b5mol L\u207b\u00b9)\n - pic \u2014 Particulate inorganic carbon (mg m\u207b\u00b3)\n - dtc \u2014 Carbon-to-nitrogen detritus (\u00b5g C L\u207b\u00b9)\n - nitrate and silicate \u2014 Dissolved nutrients (\u00b5mol L\u207b\u00b9)\n - iron \u2014 Dissolved iron (nmol L\u207b\u00b9)\n - mld \u2014 Ocean mixed-layer thickness (m)\n - par \u2014 Photosynthetically active radiation (quanta m\u207b\u00b2 d\u207b\u00b9)\n - salinity \u2014 Salinity (psu)\n - temperature \u2014 Temperature (degrees Celsius)\n - latitude, longitude, and wavelength \u2014 Spatial and spectral coordinates",
